    {
      "number": 1,
      "title": "Your Confidential NextGen Readiness Report",
      "subtitle": "",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Prepared for {{participant}} | Generated {{date}}"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Dear Participant,"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Thank you for completing the Adamas NextGen Readiness Review. This report considers your understanding of the family enterprise, your relationship with ownership, your practical experience and the responsibilities you may choose to assume."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Your reported strengths include {{model.strengths.0.label}}, {{model.strengths.1.label}}, {{model.strengths.2.label}}."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The principal priorities are {{model.priorities.0.label}}, {{model.priorities.1.label}}, {{model.priorities.2.label}}. Each finding includes a practical next step and evidence by which progress can be reviewed."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Your preparation and the family arrangements both deserve attention. Some steps are yours to take; others require information, support or a decision from an existing authority holder. A fulfilling role outside the family remains a valid choice."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Alexander"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Alexander von der Vellen"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Founder, Adamas Advisors"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "title": "How to Read Your Report",
      "subtitle": "Read the scores alongside the explanations and the practical tests.",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "kicker",
          "text": "Maturity"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Green (3/3) reflects a strong self-reported foundation. Amber (2/3) indicates developing preparation. Red (1/3) identifies limited preparation or a dependency. Grey remains unscored where responses are insufficient. A score is not a judgement of your character or an appointment to a role."
        },
        {
          "type": "kicker",
          "text": "Visibility and verification"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Reported visibility describes how completely you answered the relevant statements. It does not mean that documents or practical performance have been independently verified. Use explanations, records and supervised exercises to test your understanding."
        },
        {
          "type": "kicker",
          "text": "Understanding the gap"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Ask whether the gap concerns knowledge, access to information, practical experience, mutual expectations or a role you may not wish to take. The questionnaire can indicate where to investigate; it cannot establish the cause or another family member's views."
        },
        {
          "type": "kicker",
          "text": "Using the recommendations"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Each subdimension names the relevant question pair, explains the finding and offers an exercise with evidence of progress. Confirm a sponsor, information access and authority before acting. An unscored area should be clarified before adopting a substantive development task."
        },
        {
          "type": "kicker",
          "text": "Scoring discipline"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Both statements are needed to score a subdimension. A dimension requires at least five numeric responses and fewer than three unknown answers. Not applicable responses are excluded. Scores use unrounded averages; no overall readiness percentage is produced."
        }
      ]
    },
